{"title":"1.2. Exercises","markdown":{"yaml":{"format":"html"},"headingText":"1.2. Exercises","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n<script src='../../src/quiz.js'></script>  \n\n\n## Derivatives of Common Functions\n\n\n<div id=\"mcq1\"></div> \n<script> \ngenerateQuiz( \n    \"mcq1\", \n    \"Increasing or Decreasing?\", \n    `\n    Is the function cos(&pi; - x) increasing or decreasing at x = &pi;/2?<br><br> In other words, if the current input is &pi;/2, should we increase or decrease the input slightly if we want the output to increase?\n    `,\n    {\n        \"Increase the input slightly\": \"\",\n        \"Decrease the input slightly\": \"Try again! What is the derivative here? Can you draw a picture?\", \n        \"The function is flat at x = &pi;/2\": \"Try again! What is the derivative here? Can you draw a picture?\", \n        \"Cannot determine from the information given\": \"Try again! What is the derivative here? Can you draw a picture?\" }, \n        \"Increase the input slightly\" \n    );\n</script>\n\n<div id=\"mcq2\"></div> \n<script> \ngenerateQuiz( \n    \"mcq2\", \n    \"Where is the function not differentiable?\", \n    `\n    List all points where the functions |x| and |x|&sup2 are not differentiable.\n    `,\n    {\n        \"Both functions are differentiable everywhere\": \"Can you plot the functions? What happens near zero?\",\n        \"|x| is not differentiable at zero, but |x|&sup2 is differentiable everywhere\": \"\", \n        \"|x|&sup2 is not differentiable at zero, but |x| is differentiable everywhere\": \"Can you plot the functions? What happens near zero?\", \n        \"Neither function is differentiable at zero\": \"Can you plot the functions? What happens near zero?\" }, \n        \"|x| is not differentiable at zero, but |x|&sup2 is differentiable everywhere\" \n    );\n</script>\n\nThe following exercises are adapted from the [CLP-1 Problem Book](https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~CLP/CLP1/)\n\n<div id='mcq3'></div>\n<script>\ngenerateMultiQuiz(\n    'mcq3',\n    'Identifying linear functions',\n    `Which of the following functions describe a straight line? Select all correct options.`,\n    {\n        'y = e<sup>3 log x</sup> + 1': `Not quite a line. Can you use some rules of exponentiation to figure out why?`,\n        \n        '2y + 5 = e<sup>3 + log x</sup>': `Yep, that's a line!`,\n        \n        'y = e<sup>2x</sup> + 4': `Not quite. How does this look compared to e<sup>x</sup>?`,\n        \n        'y = e<sup>log x</sup> · 3<sup>e</sup> + log 2': `Yep, that's a line!`\n    },\n    [\n        '2y + 5 = e<sup>3 + log x</sup>',\n        'y = e<sup>log x</sup> · 3<sup>e</sup> + log 2'\n    ]\n);\n</script>\n\n<div id='mcq4'></div>\n<script>\ngenerateMultiQuiz(\n    'mcq4',\n    'Sine and cosine',\n    `Graph sine and cosine on the same axes from x = -2π to x = 2π. At which points does sin(x) have a tangent line with maximum positive slope, and what do these points correspond to on the graph of cosine?`,\n    {\n        'All multiples of π/2': 'Does this include points where sin(x) is flat?',\n        \n        'All multiples of π': 'Is sin(x) increasing or decreasing at π?',\n        \n        'All multiples of 2π': `That's right! What is the value of cos(x) here?`,\n        \n        'All points where sin(x) = 1': `Since sin(x) attains its maximum value here, what must be its derivative?`\n    },\n    [\n        'Multiples of 2π'\n    ]\n);\n</script>","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n<script src='../../src/quiz.js'></script>  \n\n# 1.2. Exercises\n\n## Derivatives of Common Functions\n\n\n<div id=\"mcq1\"></div> \n<script> \ngenerateQuiz( \n    \"mcq1\", \n    \"Increasing or Decreasing?\", \n    `\n    Is the function cos(&pi; - x) increasing or decreasing at x = &pi;/2?<br><br> In other words, if the current input is &pi;/2, should we increase or decrease the input slightly if we want the output to increase?\n    `,\n    {\n        \"Increase the input slightly\": \"\",\n        \"Decrease the input slightly\": \"Try again! What is the derivative here? Can you draw a picture?\", \n        \"The function is flat at x = &pi;/2\": \"Try again! What is the derivative here? Can you draw a picture?\", \n        \"Cannot determine from the information given\": \"Try again! What is the derivative here? Can you draw a picture?\" }, \n        \"Increase the input slightly\" \n    );\n</script>\n\n<div id=\"mcq2\"></div> \n<script> \ngenerateQuiz( \n    \"mcq2\", \n    \"Where is the function not differentiable?\", \n    `\n    List all points where the functions |x| and |x|&sup2 are not differentiable.\n    `,\n    {\n        \"Both functions are differentiable everywhere\": \"Can you plot the functions? What happens near zero?\",\n        \"|x| is not differentiable at zero, but |x|&sup2 is differentiable everywhere\": \"\", \n        \"|x|&sup2 is not differentiable at zero, but |x| is differentiable everywhere\": \"Can you plot the functions? What happens near zero?\", \n        \"Neither function is differentiable at zero\": \"Can you plot the functions? What happens near zero?\" }, \n        \"|x| is not differentiable at zero, but |x|&sup2 is differentiable everywhere\" \n    );\n</script>\n\nThe following exercises are adapted from the [CLP-1 Problem Book](https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~CLP/CLP1/)\n\n<div id='mcq3'></div>\n<script>\ngenerateMultiQuiz(\n    'mcq3',\n    'Identifying linear functions',\n    `Which of the following functions describe a straight line? Select all correct options.`,\n    {\n        'y = e<sup>3 log x</sup> + 1': `Not quite a line. Can you use some rules of exponentiation to figure out why?`,\n        \n        '2y + 5 = e<sup>3 + log x</sup>': `Yep, that's a line!`,\n        \n        'y = e<sup>2x</sup> + 4': `Not quite. How does this look compared to e<sup>x</sup>?`,\n        \n        'y = e<sup>log x</sup> · 3<sup>e</sup> + log 2': `Yep, that's a line!`\n    },\n    [\n        '2y + 5 = e<sup>3 + log x</sup>',\n        'y = e<sup>log x</sup> · 3<sup>e</sup> + log 2'\n    ]\n);\n</script>\n\n<div id='mcq4'></div>\n<script>\ngenerateMultiQuiz(\n    'mcq4',\n    'Sine and cosine',\n    `Graph sine and cosine on the same axes from x = -2π to x = 2π. At which points does sin(x) have a tangent line with maximum positive slope, and what do these points correspond to on the graph of cosine?`,\n    {\n        'All multiples of π/2': 'Does this include points where sin(x) is flat?',\n        \n        'All multiples of π': 'Is sin(x) increasing or decreasing at π?',\n        \n        'All multiples of 2π': `That's right! What is the value of cos(x) here?`,\n        \n        'All points where sin(x) = 1': `Since sin(x) attains its maximum value here, what must be its derivative?`\n    },\n    [\n        'Multiples of 2π'\n    ]\n);\n</script>"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"l